[?2004l[?2004h> ## Resume and crash recovery
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The checkpoint is a commit record for a durable prefix of live documents. Its
[?2004l[?2004h> `last_id` is exclusive on the next source query (IDs need not be contiguous).
[?2004l[?2004h> `docs` counts that prefix, and `shards` records the committed byte length of each
[?2004l[?2004h> shard. Index rows and the checksum/minhash algorithms are unchanged.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The worker retains block buffering: it fsyncs all affected shards (including
[?2004l[?2004h> rotated files), syncs the index directory, then writes and fsyncs a temporary
[?2004l[?2004h> checkpoint, atomically replaces the old checkpoint, and syncs its directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP request a stop after the current document; the worker commits
[?2004l[?2004h> that prefix and exits 75. No work or I/O is done in the signal handler.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> After an abrupt kill, the next invocation first truncates uncommitted shard tails
[?2004l[?2004h> and removes uncommitted shards using the last checkpoint. This rollback is itself
[?2004l[?2004h> restartable, and runs even for an already-complete checkpoint. Missing committed
[?2004l[?2004h> bytes or corrupt versioned checkpoints cause an error rather than silently
[?2004l[?2004h> skipping documents or discarding committed progress. Legacy checkpoints from the
[?2004l[?2004h> old worker have no reliable durable boundary, so they trigger a one-time rebuild.
[?2004l[?2004h> Use `./jobs reindex` to retain the supervisor's single-run lock; do not run workers
[?2004l[?2004h> concurrently against the same output. `./jobs clean` deliberately discards all
[?2004l[?2004h> progress and should only be used when no reindex is running.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> A completed checkpoint describes one reindex of a stable source corpus. To build
[?2004l[?2004h> a new generation after source edits/deletions, explicitly clean and reindex.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
